<newsitem itemid="449145" id="root" date="1997-03-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>USA: Hunt Manufacturing Q1 sales up, net flat.</title>
<headline>Hunt Manufacturing Q1 sales up, net flat.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					  March 2, 1997   March 3, 1996</p>
<p>Net sales				    $76,602	  $73,668</p>
<p>Income from operations before</p>
<p> special charges			    $5,501	   $5,606</p>
<p>Special charges				 (950)	    (354)</p>
<p>						 -------	  -------</p>
<p>Income from operations		    $4,551	   $5,252</p>
<p>Earnings:</p>
<p>  Income before special charges	 $2,712	   $3,056</p>
<p>  Special charges			     (622)	    (230)</p>
<p>  Gain on business divestitures	    310		 --</p>
<p>						 -------	  -------</p>
<p>  Net income				  $2,400	   $2,826</p>
<p>Earnings per common share:</p>
<p>  Income before special charges	   $.25	     $.24</p>
<p>  Special charges			     (.06)	    (.02)</p>
<p>  Gain on business divestitures	    .03		 --</p>
<p>						 -------	  -------</p>
<p>  Net income				    $.22	     $.22</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding		11,007	   12,939</p>
<p>NOTES: Q1 1997 included higher interest costs on debt incurred in connection with repurchase of common shares during Q1 1996; consulting fees related to assistance for current strategic assessment of various business segments and markets, and development of a strategic plan for the operation and direction of the company ($1.0 million pre-tax, or $0.06 per share after tax) and; net gain on divestitures of the Lit-Ning Products business and Hunt Data Products' MediaMate and Calise brand products ($500,000 pre-tax, or $0.03 per share after tax), which divestitures occurred on Feb. 28, 1997.</p>
<p>Excluding charges on both fiscal quarters, earnings per share would have been $0.25 in the Q1 1997 vs $0.24 in Q1 1996.</p>
<p>Full company name is Hunt Manufacturing Co.</p>
</text>
